## R7 - Compile Guard Boundary

Problem: Sequential `Hecton8.Core.csproj` build exposed an external compile wall in `SomaticKinematicsRuntime.cs`: missing namespace for `PhysicsDeterminismSignals`, then missing `EnsureNativeState(bool)` overload expected by existing call sites.

Solution: Added `using Hecton8.Physics;` and restored a bool overload that blocks cold initialization from hot `FixedTick` paths while preserving cold initialization in Awake/OnEnable/SlowTick/rebind paths.

Rejected Alternatives: Rewriting somatic kinematics was rejected as cross-domain sabotage. Replacing the call sites with the no-arg method was rejected because it would allow legacy file scans from hot paths.

Scalability potential: Low tier avoids cold archive/file work in `FixedTick`; middle/high/ultra keep the same deterministic state path.

Hardware Impact: Avoids accidental hot-path file/archive work; runtime gain is conditional, but worst-case spike prevention matters more than average us.
